==Usage==
{{See|Serpent's Bed of Sand}}[[Qifrey's Atelier|Qifrey's apprentices]] use a repetition seal in the [[Serpent's Bed of Sand]]. This spell is meant to create a cloud of sand that can support a large [[dragon]]. They wrap the spell in repetition magic so that even if the cloud dissipates under the weight of the dragon, it will continuously return to its original form of a fluffy cloud.{{Ref|m|7|20}}{{Ref|a|5}}

{{See|Magic Cookpot}}[[Qifrey]] uses a repetition seal on the lid of one of his cookpots. This allows it to continuously repeat the moment a cooked meal was freshly made, meaning food will not spoil so long as the seals are regularly redrawn. In the manga, it is shown to turn shriveled [[Carapace Yam|carapace yams]] into ripe ones.{{Ref|m|8|8-9}}{{Ref|a|6}}{{Ref|m|28|10}}

{{See|Washbarrels}}The baths of the [[Great Hall]] have multiples [[Washbarrels]] using repetition seals. It returns clothes that have been damaged, dirtied or embroidered into their original state.{{Ref|m|32|7}}<ref>[[:File:Birthday Sinocia.jpg]] Sinocia's Birthday Comic from 2021, in which Ermile gives Sinocia an embroidered handkerchief and therefore Sinocia refuses to wash it</ref>

{{See|Spirits Bubble}}Olruggio adapts a classic [[Vapor Bubble]] by using a repetition seal much like the Magic Cookpot, creating the contraption [[Spirits Bubble]]. It keeps whatever is inside to remain at peak flavor.{{Ref|k|10|5}}
